You never touch any other file. The `reference_test_file` in your input (originate's KS-978 spec-registry test) is shape reference only - do NOT touch it.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

The registration for `POST /api/v2/verification/verify` (`originate.openapi.ts:2026`-`:2077`) declares its request body as a multi-line `body: {` block (`:2055`-`:2059`) whose only key is `content:`, with no `required`, so the published spec says the body is OPTIONAL. The handler says otherwise: `routes/verificationV2.ts:427`-`:428` (`verificationV2Router.post('/verify', ...)`) reads `documentId, hash, providedHash, contentHash, documentHash, documentData` from `req.body || {}` (`:450`), resolves the hash as `hash || providedHash || contentHash || documentHash` (`:451`), and when there is no documentId, no hash and no documentData answers 400 "Provide a content hash (or documentData to hash), or a documentId." (`:452`-`:456`). The service mounts `express.json()` (`index.ts:103`) on express 4, which leaves `req.body` as `{}` when no body is sent, so an absent body reaches `:452` and is refused with 400. KS-1364's sweep 4 recorded 2 no-body cases for this operation, both status 400 (the sweep did not record which gate answered). The ticket's direction is verbatim: "mark `requestBody.required: true` ... at the generator (`*.openapi.ts`)". The QA gate on #1365 accepted handlers that refuse an absent body by a check other than a zod schema. In the multi-line form the house shape is a `required: true,` line as the first key inside the `body:` block (`auth.openapi.ts:1720`). The route stays PUBLIC (`security: []`, `:2029`): this marks the body required, it does not change who may call.

## Where

- `:2055` - the v2 verify body's `body: {` line; it stays, and a `required: true,` line is inserted AFTER it (insertion site)

## The exact change

ONE hunk, a PURE INSERTION of one line (old side 6, new side 7). Nothing is removed. The new line is `      required: true,` at SIX spaces, the same indent as the `content: {` line below it. Every context line is non-blank. NOTE: the v1 registration at `:1992`-`:1997` has the same lines except its schema line (`VerifyRequestSchema`); the hunk below is the v2 one (`V2VerifyRequestSchema`, `:2057`) at `@@ -2053`. Copy it exactly.

